The  iSCSI initiator runs as a kernel driver, and provides access
to iSCSI targets running across a network using the iSCSI  proto‐
col, RFC 3720.  The utility itself interfaces to the kernel iSCSI
driver,  and also communicates, using with the iSCSI name service
running on other hosts to locate services  and  iSCSI  instances.
In  normal  operation, is a standard daemon, and will detach from
the controlling terminal using and then loops, reading  requests,
processing  them,  and  sending  responses.   Communication takes
place over a Unix domain socket.  exits on receiving a  terminate
